### VendorBridge Purchase Order & Invoice API Tests
### Use REST Client extension in VS Code to run these tests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@procurementToken = YOUR_PROCUREMENT_TOKEN_HERE
@managerToken = YOUR_MANAGER_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Login as Procurement Officer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sarah.procurement@vendorbridge.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login as Manager
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mike.manager@vendorbridge.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Create Purchase Order from approved quotation
# First make sure quotation #3 has all approvals completed
# Then create PO
POST {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quotation_id": 3
}

### 4. List all Purchase Orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### 5. List Purchase Orders filtered by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders?status=approved
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### 6. List Purchase Orders filtered by vendor
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders?vendor_id=1
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### 7. Get Purchase Order detail (replace 1 with actual PO ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### 8. Update Purchase Order status to pending_payment
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "pending_payment"
}

### 9. Update Purchase Order status to paid
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "paid"
}

### 10. Get Invoice data for Purchase Order
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1/invoice
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### 11. Send Invoice to vendor (simulated email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1/send-invoice
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### ========================================
### COMPLETE WORKFLOW TEST
### ========================================

### STEP 1: Check existing quotations with full approvals
GET {{baseUrl}}/quotations/3
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### STEP 2: Create PO from fully approved quotation
POST {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quotation_id": 3
}

### STEP 3: Verify PO was created
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### STEP 4: Get full PO details
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### STEP 5: Generate invoice data
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1/invoice
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### STEP 6: Send invoice to vendor
POST {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1/send-invoice
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### STEP 7: Update status to pending_payment
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "pending_payment"
}

### STEP 8: Mark as paid
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "paid"
}

### STEP 9: Verify final status
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}

### ========================================
### ERROR SCENARIOS
### ========================================

### ERROR 1: Try to create PO from non-approved quotation
POST {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quotation_id": 1
}

### ERROR 2: Try to create PO from non-existent quotation
POST {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quotation_id": 9999
}

### ERROR 3: Try to create duplicate PO
POST {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quotation_id": 3
}

### ERROR 4: Invalid status update
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "invalid_status"
}

### ERROR 5: Get non-existent PO
GET {{baseUrl}}/purchase-orders/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{procurementToken}}
